Architectural DesignInterface Contract Signature (.NET 10) <p>The core SDK establishes an invariant contract interface (<code>IGamePlugin</code>) that all separate game plugin dynamic link libraries (DLLs) must implement. This ensures the main orchestrator can interface with any target plugin without compilation dependencies.</p> <p>Dynamic Interface Component Requirements</p> Interface Property / Method Returns / Parameters Target Architectural Purpose <code>TargetProcessCommName</code> <code>string</code> Matches the Linux kernel's 16-byte <code>process_comm</code> tag array dynamically. <code>PluginVersionSignature</code> <code>string</code> Pins build versions to avoid out-of-date pointer execution crashes. <code>ExecuteIntrospection</code> <code>void</code> Accepts primitive virtualization base coordinates passed downward from the Core engine. <pre><code>namespace MuMuSDK.Core.Interfaces
{
    public interface IGamePlugin
    {
        string TargetProcessCommName { get; } // (1)
        string PluginVersionSignature { get; } // (2)
        void ExecuteIntrospection(ulong pgdBaseGpa, IntPtr upperRamHva); // (3)
    }
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li>🔍 Explicit process tag used by the dynamic runtime loader to match active running packages.</li> <li>🛡️ Verification fingerprint used to block execution paths if the underlying game pushes a new update.</li> <li>⚡ The primary execution entry hook invoked by the host presentation orchestrator.</li> </ol>
